/*
 * NARM Studio v0.14.2 - cached cursor overlay
 *
 * Built with the user-provided NARMCC API 1.9 optimizer compiler at -O3.
 *
 * v0.14.2 changes:
 *   - keeps a packed 4-bit shadow of the static timeline pixels
 *   - restores the old cursor and timestamp directly from that pixel shadow
 *   - performs no note, clip, waveform, file, or voice scans during playback
 *   - computes the playback end frame once instead of rescanning the project
 *
 * v0.14.1 changes:
 *   - restores the full-height timeline cursor and time badge during playback
 *   - reconstructs only the narrow area beneath the previous cursor overlay
 *     so the cached/static UI optimization remains active
 *
 * v0.14.0 changes:
 *   - batches each small-text string into one VGA4 glyph submission
 *   - caches visible waveform peaks as four 523-column screen rows
 *   - redraws only the playback clock and position markers at 33.3 Hz
 *   - page-scrolls during playback so static timeline layers remain reusable
 *
 * v0.13.3 changes:
 *   - restores full UI redraws at a 30 ms cadence during playback
 *   - removes the artificial 1/2 ms playback sleeps added while diagnosing
 *     the unrelated firmware SD-lock starvation bug
 *   - keeps cooperative yields so firmware services remain responsive without
 *     imposing a fixed delay inside the drawing path
 *
 * v0.13.2 changes:
 *   - fixes Studio-generated WAV RIFF/data length serialization above 16 MiB
 *   - verifies all 32 bits of preview.wav RIFF/data sizes from SD before playback
 *   - retains starvation diagnostics without attributing the bug to UI redraw
 *   - retains v0.13's 2048-note capacity and NARMCC -O3 build
 *
 * Key changes:
 *   - synth tracks no longer contain built-in demo notes in a new project
 *   - N/Enter on a synth track opens a piano-roll note editor
 *   - Enter inserts notes; Delete removes them; Up/Down selects pitch
 *   - project timeline is runtime-sized, starts at 60 s and auto-expands
 *   - rendered audio length follows actual content, so empty timeline does not cost render time
 *   - SPACE toggles play/pause and resumes from the exact cursor frame
 *   - playing from the end wraps to frame 0 instead of returning an error
 *   - LEFT/RIGHT cursor movement accelerates exponentially after 2 seconds held
 *   - waveform is a high-contrast 1-pixel outline, not filled peak blocks
 *   - waveform cache resolution remains adjustable per selected audio track
 *   - audio WAVs are selected with an SD-root browser instead of a hard-coded path
 *   - audio tracks keep their own source WAV path/RIFF metadata
 *   - tracks are dynamic: only real tracks are shown, plus one ADD TRACK row
 *   - each track has a visible X remove control; Delete/Backspace activates it
 *   - Add Track chooses SYNTH or AUDIO; AUDIO immediately opens the WAV browser
 *   - E exports the current premix to the active project folder
 *   - DSP blocks remain 32768 frames, but firmware file transfers are bounded to 32 KiB and tolerate partial transfers
 *   - frame-zero playback uses the cached preview directly; no duplicate playback WAV copy
 *   - API 1.8 frame-seek playback starts directly inside preview/source WAVs; no cursor-to-EOF copy
 *   - untouched single-WAV projects bypass rendering entirely and play the source directly
 *   - render progress redraws are throttled and the artificial per-block sleep is gone
 *   - rendered WAV size/header are verified before playback
 *   - synth release begins at the exact stored note length, including note-off during attack/decay
 */

